{"availability":"available","full":"Project-MONAI/monai-physio","name":"monai-physio","description":"Generate anatomic models in Omniverse with physiological motion derived from medical images.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":93,"forks":16,"created":"2025-12-05T13:08:16Z","updated":"2026-10-08T08:50:12Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://project-monai.github.io/monai-physio/","topics":[],"demo":"https://project-monai.github.io/monai-physio/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T05:49:21.400Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T05:49:21.400Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T05:49:21.400Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T05:49:21.400Z","stars":93,"forks":16}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A collection of methods, workflows, tutorials, and CLI tools for creating personalized physiological digital twins.","MONAI Physio typically begins with a 3D medical image of a subject, extracts anatomic models from that image, and then uses AI surrogates to estimate the subject's physiological processes - initially focusing on cardiac and respiratory motion, and expanding to electrophysiology, blood flow, and organ perfusion. The package provides methods for forming these physiological AI surrogates and for finetuning the segmentation and registration AI methods that power them, with special emphasis on statistical shape models: they capture subject-specific characteristics that help determine…","MONAI Physio is not validated for clinical use. It is a research and visualization toolkit, not a medical device, and must not be used for diagnosis, treatment planning, or clinical decision-making."],"features":["Personalized digital twins: build subject-specific anatomic models and physiological AI surrogates from 3D/4D medical images","Statistical shape models: capture subject-specific anatomy and establish cross-subject correspondence, aiding AI surrogate generalization and simplifying traditional solver setup","Simplified workflows on industry-leading open-source tools: ICON and Greedy for registration; MONAI with TotalSegmentator and Simpleware for segmentation; scikit-learn for statistical shape modeling; ITK for image…","Extensible class hierarchy: add new segmentation and registration methods, and extend to new data types, organs, and physiological processes, without reworking the workflow layer","Physiological motion: cardiac and respiratory motion today, expanding to electrophysiology, blood flow, and organ perfusion"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Project-MONAI/monai-physio/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2e76971fdf623594f64bda77ab53df60f47ef8c7a3e3de7cb8ff27504ee14e82","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T05:49:21.550Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T05:49:21.550Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A collection of methods, workflows, tutorials, and CLI tools for creating personalized physiological digital twins.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Project-MONAI/monai-physio/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"2e76971fdf623594f64bda77ab53df60f47ef8c7a3e3de7cb8ff27504ee14e82","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Project-MONAI/monai-physio/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T05:49:21.550Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T08:50:12Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Project-MONAI/monai-physio/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T05:49:21.550Z","hash":"2e76971fdf623594f64bda77ab53df60f47ef8c7a3e3de7cb8ff27504ee14e82","originalBytes":9454,"storedBytes":9454,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["tutorials","data","license","workflow","physiological","registration","segmentation","tutorial","images","models","monai","see","download","nvidia","physio","python","series","time","tools","usd","workflows","cardiac","class","cli","e.g.","heart","image","methods","path","shape","statistical","subject-specific","surrogates","use.","api","clinical","co